## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`getEntry`): This is the central content-fetching function (12 callers across pageService, directoryService, redirectsService, serviceUpdatesService) that constructs Contentstack SDK queries. The Stack is already initialized with live_preview config (lines 69-72, reading CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW env var), but getEntry and ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeQuery never call Stack.livePreviewQuery() or forward live preview hash/token to the SDK query — so draft content from the CMS can never be fetched, making live preview non-functional regardless of client-side wiring.
  - **Minimal fix:** In getEntry, accept a livePreviewQuery parameter (the raw request query object from getServerSideProps/getStaticProps). Before creating the ContentType query, call Stack.livePreviewQuery(livePreviewQuery) to inject the preview hash into the Stack instance. Then the existing query.find() calls will automatically include draft content when a valid live_preview token is present. Propagate the parameter through ICreateQueryConfig and IContentstackGetEntry interfaces. The helper is Stack.livePreviewQuery — it is a method on the already-exported Stack object in this same file (line 75: export const Stack = contentstack.Stack(options)).


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a CMS editor opens the site from the CMS's live preview panel, the rendered page displays the draft (unpublished) version of the entry's content rather than the currently published version.
- After a CMS editor changes a field on an entry and saves it as a draft, the page shown in the CMS preview panel reflects the edited value without the editor manually reloading the browser page.
- A draft edit to an entry used by a standard page is visible on that page when viewed through the CMS preview, while the same URL opened in a normal browser session continues to show the previously published content.
- A draft edit to a directory listing entry is visible on the directory page when viewed through the CMS preview, while the public directory page continues to show the published listing.
- A draft edit to a service update entry is visible on the service updates display when viewed through the CMS preview, while the public view continues to show the published update.
- A draft edit to a redirect entry takes effect when navigating the site through the CMS preview, while normal site navigation continues to follow the published redirect behaviour.
- Pages render completely and without visible error messages or broken layout both when viewed through the CMS preview panel and when viewed as a normal site visitor.
- Content that exists only as a draft and has never been published is visible on the page when viewed through the CMS preview, and is absent from the page when viewed as a normal site visitor.

